{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For multiplication.</b> The way of the Scribes' derash is that the mem is closed within the word, though it ought to be at the end — an allusion to the sun's sign when the shadow turned back. It is possible that מרבה is a noun like מעשה, or a verb from the heavy [piel] stem that is augmented:" "<b>In judgment.</b> And so it is written there:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:58.206633533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}